WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:07.424 --> 00:00:10.885
Subtitles are color-coded by country,
and this setting cannot be changed.

2
00:00:27.110 --> 00:00:31.364
HISTORY TOOK SHAPE THROUGH THE HUMAN BODY

3
00:00:35.744 --> 00:00:37.996
We compete until
we have nothing left to give.

4
00:00:38.788 --> 00:00:40.582
Whoever makes it through,
we'll crush them.

5
00:00:40.665 --> 00:00:41.916
Get off it.

6
00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:43.501
THE HUMAN BODY WAS BOTH SPEAR AND SHIELD

7
00:00:43.585 --> 00:00:47.505
They may look intimidating,
but they're actually easy prey.

8
00:00:48.923 --> 00:00:51.509
No one takes this from us, no one.

9
00:00:51.593 --> 00:00:53.344
AND A MEANS TO SEIZE LIFE

10
00:00:57.766 --> 00:01:00.060
We came here to win the championship.

11
00:01:01.561 --> 00:01:03.605
UNDER THE FLAGS OF EIGHT COUNTRIES

12
00:01:03.688 --> 00:01:04.898
Let's go!

13
00:01:04.981 --> 00:01:06.316
Go, go, go, it's time. Let's go!

14
00:01:06.399 --> 00:01:08.735
ONLY THE COUNTRY
THAT EMBODIES THE PERFECT PHYSIQUE

15
00:01:08.818 --> 00:01:12.489
In honor of our country,
we will crush them and come out on top.

16
00:01:12.572 --> 00:01:15.450
We are a people born to fight and to win.

17
00:01:18.369 --> 00:01:21.081
WILL BE ACCORDED A NEW PLACE IN HISTORY

18
00:01:21.164 --> 00:01:23.166
It was like watching a slow death.

19
00:01:24.709 --> 00:01:27.921
It was a level of pain
that I had never experienced before.

20
00:01:28.880 --> 00:01:32.008
But we just take on
whatever comes on towards us.

21
00:01:32.091 --> 00:01:33.468
Headstrong, head first.

22
00:01:33.551 --> 00:01:35.136
That's one spirit that we have.

23
00:01:36.012 --> 00:01:37.889
We're strong and it's in our blood.

24
00:01:39.349 --> 00:01:40.892
This is not a game,

25
00:01:42.143 --> 00:01:43.269
but war.

26
00:01:44.229 --> 00:01:45.063
No mercy,

27
00:01:46.481 --> 00:01:47.440
no surrender,

28
00:01:48.399 --> 00:01:49.317
to the death.

29
00:01:50.610 --> 00:01:51.653
Let's go!

30
00:01:53.029 --> 00:01:53.947
Attack!

31
00:01:55.156 --> 00:02:01.621
PHYSICAL: ASIA

32
00:02:03.832 --> 00:02:09.129
1. WHERE THE SUN RISES

33
00:02:58.887 --> 00:03:00.889
The contestants
who've watched the previous seasons

34
00:03:00.972 --> 00:03:02.307
will try to keep us down, I'm sure.

35
00:03:05.894 --> 00:03:09.772
I think physically, we'll hold our own
against the other countries.

36
00:03:13.109 --> 00:03:16.738
What's certain is that this season
will be different from the previous ones.

37
00:03:16.821 --> 00:03:17.864
Very different.

38
00:03:29.292 --> 00:03:30.335
My gosh.

39
00:03:33.004 --> 00:03:33.838
Hello.

40
00:03:33.922 --> 00:03:36.132
I'm Korea's first-ever UFC fighter,
Kim Dong-hyun.

41
00:03:36.215 --> 00:03:37.050
Pleased to meet you.

42
00:03:37.133 --> 00:03:38.384
KIM DONG-HYUN
MMA FIGHTER

43
00:03:39.218 --> 00:03:42.347
My career record is 28 matches,
with 22 wins and 4 losses.

44
00:03:42.430 --> 00:03:45.975
I've only ever lost four times
in the UFC welterweight division.

45
00:03:46.684 --> 00:03:50.188
I think the ultimate sport
for proving who the toughest is

46
00:03:50.271 --> 00:03:51.689
has to be the UFC.

47
00:03:51.773 --> 00:03:53.858
Physical: Asia is another chance

48
00:03:53.942 --> 00:03:57.403
for me to prove
how strong I am physically,

49
00:03:57.487 --> 00:03:59.239
so I'm ready to go all out.

50
00:03:59.322 --> 00:04:03.201
The disappointment of being eliminated
from Physical: 100 Season 2

51
00:04:03.284 --> 00:04:05.620
still haunts me in my dreams sometimes.

52
00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:07.914
We have to place second!

53
00:04:07.997 --> 00:04:10.124
Hang your legs.

54
00:04:14.420 --> 00:04:15.880
I should've done it.

55
00:04:15.964 --> 00:04:17.757
It was a gut-wrenching defeat.

56
00:04:18.383 --> 00:04:20.843
I still remember the speech I made
when I smashed my torso.

57
00:04:20.927 --> 00:04:24.472
I'm going back to the body I had
in my fighting days.

58
00:04:25.682 --> 00:04:27.934
I swore I'd never be
that out of shape again.

59
00:04:29.143 --> 00:04:31.980
After Physical: 100,
I turned over a new leaf

60
00:04:32.063 --> 00:04:34.107
and started an intense workout regimen.

61
00:04:35.525 --> 00:04:37.944
Having once tasted bitter defeat,

62
00:04:38.611 --> 00:04:43.574
I'm back, resolutely determined
to never lose again,

63
00:04:43.658 --> 00:04:47.620
and I'm going to show you
how dangerous I can be with this mindset.

64
00:04:48.329 --> 00:04:49.205
My gosh.

65
00:04:51.874 --> 00:04:53.251
Man, I've got goosebumps.

66
00:04:53.960 --> 00:04:54.794
Hello.

67
00:04:54.877 --> 00:04:56.671
I'm CrossFit enthusiast Amotti,

68
00:04:56.754 --> 00:05:00.008
the winner of Physical: 100 Season 2.

69
00:05:00.091 --> 00:05:03.344
I'm the only Season 2 contestant
who took part in all the games,

70
00:05:03.970 --> 00:05:05.388
from the advantage challenge…

71
00:05:08.766 --> 00:05:11.060
right through to the final.

72
00:05:11.144 --> 00:05:12.145
Amotti!

73
00:05:12.228 --> 00:05:13.479
So I'm ready for anything,

74
00:05:14.022 --> 00:05:15.481
and I know I can take it all on.

75
00:05:19.193 --> 00:05:20.570
I'm Yun Sung-bin,

76
00:05:20.653 --> 00:05:23.489
a former national team skeleton racer
and an Olympic gold medalist.

77
00:05:26.075 --> 00:05:27.577
They really went all out.

78
00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:30.872
I'm Jang Eun-sil, a former member
of the women's national wrestling team.

79
00:05:30.955 --> 00:05:33.416
If you've watched Physical: 100 Season 1…

80
00:05:33.499 --> 00:05:36.169
You'll obviously be familiar with us.

81
00:05:36.878 --> 00:05:39.589
The man with the crazy physique,
Yun Sung-bin.

82
00:05:47.221 --> 00:05:50.058
I'm sure you're already well aware
of how strong I am.

83
00:05:51.059 --> 00:05:55.438
Watching it on a screen
and battling it out in person

84
00:05:55.521 --> 00:05:56.981
are two completely different things,

85
00:05:57.065 --> 00:05:58.399
as you'll soon find out.

86
00:05:58.483 --> 00:06:01.069
We'll show you how fierce Koreans can be.

87
00:06:03.279 --> 00:06:06.157
Australia, Thailand, and Indonesia, is it?

88
00:06:06.240 --> 00:06:07.366
Indonesia.

89
00:06:07.450 --> 00:06:08.951
Türkiye and Japan.

90
00:06:09.035 --> 00:06:10.369
-Mongolia.
-Mongolia.

91
00:06:10.453 --> 00:06:11.871
-The Philippines.
-The Philippines.

92
00:06:14.290 --> 00:06:15.541
Wow, this is amazing.

93
00:06:16.250 --> 00:06:18.461
Shall we check out everyone's torsos?

94
00:06:18.544 --> 00:06:21.881
Anyone know anything
about Australian CrossFitters?

95
00:06:21.964 --> 00:06:23.299
Katelin.

96
00:06:23.382 --> 00:06:24.717
-Is she famous?
-Katelin?

97
00:06:24.801 --> 00:06:25.968
Is she famous?

98
00:06:26.052 --> 00:06:27.011
Not as famous as me.

99
00:06:27.720 --> 00:06:30.890
-I like the confidence.
-Good one.

100
00:06:30.973 --> 00:06:33.059
Well, this is Physical: Asia, right?

101
00:06:33.142 --> 00:06:34.519
I'm number one in Asia,
so who'd be here, if not me?

102
00:06:34.602 --> 00:06:35.520
CHOI SEUNG-YEON
CROSSFIT ATHLETE

103
00:06:36.104 --> 00:06:37.480
CrossFit Games
is a worldwide CrossFit event.

104
00:06:37.563 --> 00:06:40.024
To qualify for it,

105
00:06:40.108 --> 00:06:46.239
you need to be
in the top two or three in Asia,

106
00:06:46.322 --> 00:06:47.990
and I made the cut.

107
00:06:48.783 --> 00:06:52.912
I participated in 2021, 2022, and 2024,

108
00:06:53.788 --> 00:06:58.084
and I'm the first Korean
to have attended the Games three times.

109
00:06:59.919 --> 00:07:01.838
There isn't a single CrossFitter out there

110
00:07:01.921 --> 00:07:06.008
who won't have heard of
Seung-yeon's achievements.

111
00:07:06.801 --> 00:07:09.095
I'm so glad she's on our team.
Out of everyone,

112
00:07:09.178 --> 00:07:10.888
she's the one I can count on the most.

113
00:07:10.972 --> 00:07:12.557
She's an all-rounder in my view.

114
00:07:13.808 --> 00:07:15.560
All right. I like that spirit.

115
00:07:15.643 --> 00:07:16.894
Let's all adopt that attitude.

116
00:07:18.229 --> 00:07:19.313
Dong-hyun.

117
00:07:19.397 --> 00:07:20.398
Here's Whittaker.

118
00:07:21.482 --> 00:07:22.483
Here's Whittaker.

119
00:07:25.194 --> 00:07:26.112
The Whittaker?

120
00:07:27.864 --> 00:07:29.532
He's a UFC champion.

121
00:07:29.615 --> 00:07:31.117
-Sorry?
-He's a champion.

122
00:07:31.200 --> 00:07:32.785
And he's still active.

123
00:07:32.869 --> 00:07:36.038
Never in my wildest dreams

124
00:07:36.122 --> 00:07:37.957
did I think I'd see him here.

125
00:07:39.167 --> 00:07:40.501
I was blown away.

126
00:07:40.585 --> 00:07:43.171
It spoke to the sheer scale
of Physical: Asia.

127
00:07:43.254 --> 00:07:45.506
I thought,
"They've seriously gone all out."

128
00:07:46.132 --> 00:07:47.717
As this is a competition of countries,

129
00:07:47.800 --> 00:07:49.760
I have high hopes about how strong

130
00:07:49.844 --> 00:07:52.388
and famous the contestants will be.

131
00:07:54.182 --> 00:07:55.057
Japan.

132
00:07:55.141 --> 00:07:57.977
Frankly speaking, there's no
MMA fighter in Asia who's on my level.

133
00:07:58.519 --> 00:07:59.979
Apart from one.

134
00:08:07.737 --> 00:08:10.031
A guy called Yushin Okami.

135
00:08:11.949 --> 00:08:13.951
He's very famous
for being a tough fighter.

136
00:08:15.119 --> 00:08:18.998
I used to have the most wins in Asia,
but Okami overtook me by one,

137
00:08:19.081 --> 00:08:21.209
so it's now 14 wins to him and 13 to me.

138
00:08:21.292 --> 00:08:22.793
I'm now second in total wins.

139
00:08:24.462 --> 00:08:25.963
Your rival is here.

140
00:08:26.047 --> 00:08:27.715
Wow, so he's here.

141
00:08:30.593 --> 00:08:31.427
Oh, the Philippines.

142
00:08:31.511 --> 00:08:32.470
Huh? 102 kg?

143
00:08:32.553 --> 00:08:34.805
-102 kg?
-Justin Coveney?

144
00:08:34.889 --> 00:08:36.766
There are actually 2 people over 100 kg.

145
00:08:37.308 --> 00:08:38.601
This guy is 140 kg.

146
00:08:39.143 --> 00:08:41.062
-140 kg?
-Wow, there's someone who's 140 kg.

147
00:08:43.397 --> 00:08:44.440
140 kg?

148
00:08:45.691 --> 00:08:48.569
He's your guy, Min-jae.

149
00:08:49.445 --> 00:08:51.822
I guess Min-jae can take on Ray then.

150
00:08:53.824 --> 00:08:57.370
I'm 190 cm tall, and I weigh 140 kg.

151
00:08:57.453 --> 00:09:00.957
I'm in the heaviest division in ssireum,
the Baekdu division.

152
00:09:01.040 --> 00:09:01.958
KIM MIN-JAE
SSIREUM WRESTLER

153
00:09:02.583 --> 00:09:04.794
My nickname is
the "Monster of the Sand Mat."

154
00:09:05.503 --> 00:09:09.590
I'm currently the wrestler
with the most wins in my weight class.

155
00:09:10.341 --> 00:09:11.842
Ssireum represents Korea,

156
00:09:11.926 --> 00:09:13.553
and I represent ssireum.

157
00:09:14.637 --> 00:09:17.765
As a proud ssireum wrestler,
I'm here to lead South Korea to victory.

158
00:09:22.812 --> 00:09:24.021
Here we go. It's happening.

159
00:09:24.105 --> 00:09:25.523
Man, I'm so nervous.

160
00:09:26.065 --> 00:09:27.149
Oh, here they come.

161
00:09:27.775 --> 00:09:28.818
Who are they?

162
00:09:34.031 --> 00:09:36.325
I was born to fight.

163
00:09:37.910 --> 00:09:40.621
When it comes to sports,
you can't top Japan.

164
00:09:41.247 --> 00:09:43.082
It's the land of martial arts, after all.

165
00:09:43.624 --> 00:09:44.667
-Who are they?
-Which country is that?

166
00:09:47.545 --> 00:09:48.796
Dong-hyun's here.

167
00:09:48.879 --> 00:09:50.381
I knew he would be here.

168
00:09:51.007 --> 00:09:52.133
I was hoping he'd be here.

169
00:09:52.216 --> 00:09:55.011
I'm the Japanese Titan, Yushin Okami.

170
00:09:55.094 --> 00:09:57.263
I've been an MMA fighter for 23 years.

171
00:09:59.724 --> 00:10:02.018
I have 14 UFC wins,

172
00:10:02.101 --> 00:10:04.979
more than any other Asian fighter.

173
00:10:05.062 --> 00:10:06.439
Nobody's topped that yet.

174
00:10:12.820 --> 00:10:14.447
A fun fact about me is…

175
00:10:14.530 --> 00:10:16.365
So there's a manga series
called Attack on Titan,

176
00:10:16.449 --> 00:10:20.870
and I was told the Titan form
of the main character

177
00:10:20.953 --> 00:10:22.622
was modeled after me.

178
00:10:24.582 --> 00:10:26.667
Even now,
no active Japanese fighter can beat him.

179
00:10:27.418 --> 00:10:29.128
-Hello.
-Hello.

180
00:10:29.211 --> 00:10:33.049
-Annyeonghaseyo.
-Annyeonghaseyo.

181
00:10:33.132 --> 00:10:34.342
Okami.

182
00:10:34.425 --> 00:10:35.676
Pleased to meet you.

183
00:10:37.470 --> 00:10:40.514
I'm definitely keen to fight
Korea's Kim Dong-hyun

184
00:10:40.598 --> 00:10:43.267
to prove how strong I am.

185
00:10:43.351 --> 00:10:44.769
I want to beat him

186
00:10:44.852 --> 00:10:46.520
and notch up another win,

187
00:10:46.604 --> 00:10:48.814
so prepare to see me
at my absolute strongest.

188
00:10:48.898 --> 00:10:50.316
-Good luck.
-Good luck.

189
00:10:50.399 --> 00:10:52.151
-Good luck.
-Good luck.

190
00:10:52.777 --> 00:10:53.944
This guy's good-looking.

191
00:10:54.028 --> 00:10:55.571
You're handsome.

192
00:10:55.655 --> 00:10:56.864
You too.

193
00:10:56.947 --> 00:10:58.282
-Wrestling?
-No, swimming.

194
00:10:58.366 --> 00:10:59.408
-Swimming.
-Yeah.

195
00:10:59.492 --> 00:11:02.119
I'm Katsumi Nakamura,
the sole national record holder

196
00:11:03.371 --> 00:11:04.497
in the 100-meter freestyle.

197
00:11:04.580 --> 00:11:07.124
KATSUMI NAKAMURA
NATIONAL TEAM SWIMMER

198
00:11:07.208 --> 00:11:09.377
Are you an MMA fighter?

199
00:11:09.460 --> 00:11:10.795
I'm an MMA fighter.

200
00:11:10.878 --> 00:11:13.881
I'm MMA fighter Kana Watanabe.

201
00:11:13.964 --> 00:11:15.508
So that's what you do.

202
00:11:16.384 --> 00:11:18.386
-Nice to meet you.
-Baseball.

203
00:11:18.469 --> 00:11:19.970
Baseball.

204
00:11:20.054 --> 00:11:21.347
I used to be a baseball player.

205
00:11:22.348 --> 00:11:23.933
Annyeonghaseyo.

206
00:11:24.642 --> 00:11:28.145
My name is Yoshio Itoi,
and I'm a former baseball player.

207
00:11:28.854 --> 00:11:32.733
It's a home run! That one went way out!

208
00:11:32.817 --> 00:11:34.777
I used to play as a batter.

209
00:11:35.528 --> 00:11:38.906
My nickname is Superman.

210
00:11:41.992 --> 00:11:43.369
I've also been a stolen base leader,

211
00:11:43.452 --> 00:11:47.748
and I'm still confident
when it comes to power and speed.

212
00:11:47.832 --> 00:11:50.334
For those two things, I'm your go-to man.

213
00:11:51.085 --> 00:11:52.878
"Superman."

214
00:11:54.338 --> 00:11:56.090
-Wrestling?
-Wrestling.

215
00:11:56.173 --> 00:11:57.216
I'm a wrestler.

216
00:11:57.716 --> 00:11:59.009
What weight class are you in?

217
00:11:59.093 --> 00:12:00.344
-You mean kilos?
-Weight.

218
00:12:00.428 --> 00:12:03.764
During the Olympics, 68 kg. Now, 65 kg.

219
00:12:03.848 --> 00:12:04.807
Hello.

220
00:12:04.890 --> 00:12:07.810
I'm Nonoka Ozaki,
a national team wrestler.

221
00:12:07.893 --> 00:12:12.022
I won bronze
in the women's freestyle 68 kg

222
00:12:12.106 --> 00:12:13.941
at the 2024 Paris Olympics.

223
00:12:16.235 --> 00:12:17.987
-Nice to meet you.
-Nice to meet you.

224
00:12:18.070 --> 00:12:19.905
When it comes to women's wrestling,

225
00:12:19.989 --> 00:12:21.991
Japan is actually the best in the world.

226
00:12:22.074 --> 00:12:25.202
I thought,
"She's not going to be easy to beat."

227
00:12:25.286 --> 00:12:26.162
Judo.

228
00:12:26.245 --> 00:12:27.288
-Nice to meet you.
-Hello.

229
00:12:27.371 --> 00:12:28.622
Paris Olympics medalist.

230
00:12:28.706 --> 00:12:29.540
A medalist?

231
00:12:29.623 --> 00:12:31.375
-Silver and bronze.
-Silver medalist.

232
00:12:32.668 --> 00:12:33.669
Paris Olympics.

233
00:12:33.752 --> 00:12:36.630
I'm Soichi Hashimoto,
the captain of the Japanese judo team.

234
00:12:37.381 --> 00:12:39.967
I won two medals at the Paris Olympics.

235
00:12:40.050 --> 00:12:41.802
"Adaptability triumphs over strength."

236
00:12:41.886 --> 00:12:44.263
It means you use your opponent's strength
to take them down.

237
00:12:46.932 --> 00:12:48.893
So Dong-hyun better watch out.

238
00:12:50.519 --> 00:12:52.146
She won bronze,
and he won silver and bronze.

239
00:12:52.229 --> 00:12:54.148
The Olympians are out in force.

240
00:12:55.316 --> 00:12:57.735
Japan…

241
00:12:59.987 --> 00:13:01.280
strong!

242
00:13:02.698 --> 00:13:03.824
Korea, strong!

243
00:13:03.908 --> 00:13:04.950
-Yeah!
-Yeah!

244
00:13:05.034 --> 00:13:06.118
-Yeah!
-Strong.

245
00:13:06.202 --> 00:13:08.621
That was a bit too cute to be threatening.

246
00:13:08.704 --> 00:13:09.622
Cute.

247
00:13:09.705 --> 00:13:11.540
Oh no, we've been called "cute."

248
00:13:11.624 --> 00:13:12.833
-Cute?
-Did he say "cute"?

249
00:13:12.917 --> 00:13:15.419
If you dare underestimate us,
you'll pay for it.

250
00:13:15.503 --> 00:13:17.338
We'll see you in the final then.

251
00:13:17.421 --> 00:13:20.382
-Final match.
-Oh, final match. Yeah.

252
00:13:20.925 --> 00:13:22.218
-Japan versus Korea.
-Good luck.

253
00:13:22.301 --> 00:13:24.887
Japan versus Korea, rivals.

254
00:13:24.970 --> 00:13:27.723
In a physical face-off
between Japan and Korea…

255
00:13:27.806 --> 00:13:28.849
Obviously, we'll win.

256
00:13:30.100 --> 00:13:32.645
-Korea versus Japan.
