Manny Pacquiao!

759
00:41:20.311 --> 00:41:23.022
I became a champion
in eight different weight divisions.

760
00:41:23.564 --> 00:41:25.483
I'm still passionate about boxing.

761
00:41:25.566 --> 00:41:28.903
That's why I'm still accepting fights.

762
00:41:28.986 --> 00:41:32.031
Then I heard about Physical: Asia,

763
00:41:32.114 --> 00:41:33.282
and I said,

764
00:41:33.365 --> 00:41:34.450
"Okay, why not?"

765
00:41:34.533 --> 00:41:37.912
My body's still strong,
so I can still fight.

766
00:41:40.122 --> 00:41:42.416
Hey, the Philippines has a good lineup.

767
00:41:42.500 --> 00:41:43.501
They have a sambo athlete.

768
00:41:43.584 --> 00:41:45.252
Oh, sambo. He used to be an MMA fighter.

769
00:41:45.336 --> 00:41:46.253
-Oh, really?
-Yes.

770
00:41:47.880 --> 00:41:50.758
My name is Mark Mugen,
a combat sambo champion.

771
00:41:51.467 --> 00:41:54.553
I've always believed
that I'm one of the strongest,

772
00:41:55.346 --> 00:41:57.640
and I couldn't say no to the opportunity.

773
00:41:58.390 --> 00:42:00.768
I think we have
a very strong, balanced team.

774
00:42:01.352 --> 00:42:03.646
We have a Philippine strongman.

775
00:42:03.729 --> 00:42:06.106
I think he's the biggest Filipino
I've ever seen.

776
00:42:06.190 --> 00:42:08.275
Rugby player, JC.

777
00:42:08.359 --> 00:42:09.944
He's very big and strong.

778
00:42:10.027 --> 00:42:12.238
He's on our national rugby team,
the Volcanoes.

779
00:42:12.321 --> 00:42:13.322
JUSTIN COVENEY
NATIONAL TEAM RUGBY PLAYER

780
00:42:13.405 --> 00:42:18.410
Robyn is a 400 m hurdle champion,

781
00:42:18.494 --> 00:42:21.330
and Robyn's very fast and explosive.

782
00:42:22.206 --> 00:42:24.875
Lara is a CrossFit champion.

783
00:42:25.918 --> 00:42:27.670
LARA
CROSSFIT ATHLETE

784
00:42:27.753 --> 00:42:33.008
We want to show the world
the determination and talent of Filipinos.

785
00:42:33.092 --> 00:42:33.968
Let's fight!

786
00:42:34.051 --> 00:42:35.511
-Philippines!
-Philippines!

787
00:42:35.594 --> 00:42:36.637
Let's go!

788
00:42:43.185 --> 00:42:44.436
-Shall we go over?
-Let's go over.

789
00:42:44.520 --> 00:42:45.771
-Let's go say hello.
-Let's go.

790
00:42:45.854 --> 00:42:48.023
Let's go say hello to the big man.

791
00:42:48.691 --> 00:42:50.150
I need to shake his hand.

792
00:42:50.234 --> 00:42:52.111
-It's an opportunity of a lifetime.
-Let's go.

793
00:42:52.194 --> 00:42:54.738
I'm a big fan of Pacquiao.

794
00:42:55.823 --> 00:42:58.200
-Everyone wants to shake Manny's hand.
-Everyone wants to go see him.

795
00:43:00.828 --> 00:43:02.913
-Big fan. Nice to meet you.
-Nice to meet you.

796
00:43:03.455 --> 00:43:04.790
Legend. A legend of legends.

797
00:43:04.873 --> 00:43:05.958
Hi guys.

798
00:43:06.041 --> 00:43:07.084
Big fan.

799
00:43:07.793 --> 00:43:10.129
Hello, big fan, brother. Jesus bless.

800
00:43:10.963 --> 00:43:12.047
Oh, it's the legend.

801
00:43:14.717 --> 00:43:16.051
He's a superstar.

802
00:43:16.594 --> 00:43:19.305
-Well, are we all here now?
-I can't believe Manny Pacquiao is here.

803
00:43:19.388 --> 00:43:20.889
There are so many superstars.

804
00:43:23.267 --> 00:43:25.728
We're here to win the championship.

805
00:43:25.811 --> 00:43:29.607
All our opponents must give it their all.

806
00:43:29.690 --> 00:43:34.612
We will seize victory
in the challenges we face.

807
00:43:41.327 --> 00:43:43.162
Physical: Asia.

808
00:43:48.000 --> 00:43:49.627
The Republic of Korea.

809
00:43:51.503 --> 00:43:52.838
I'm getting chills.

810
00:43:55.132 --> 00:43:56.175
Japan.

811
00:43:59.803 --> 00:44:00.846
Thailand.

812
00:44:03.891 --> 00:44:04.975
Mongolia.

813
00:44:10.189 --> 00:44:11.482
Indonesia.

814
00:44:15.194 --> 00:44:16.779
Türkiye.

815
00:44:21.700 --> 00:44:22.743
Australia.

816
00:44:28.499 --> 00:44:29.667
The Philippines.

817
00:44:33.712 --> 00:44:38.008
Welcome,
contestants from all eight countries.

818
00:44:38.092 --> 00:44:41.303
-Hello.
-Hello.

819
00:44:46.809 --> 00:44:50.521
You have gathered here,
representing your countries

820
00:44:51.146 --> 00:44:52.439
with your physiques.

821
00:44:53.649 --> 00:44:55.150
Physical: Asia

822
00:44:55.234 --> 00:44:58.695
is a country-versus-country
team competition

823
00:44:58.779 --> 00:45:01.407
with six contestants
representing each country.

824
00:45:02.908 --> 00:45:04.535
Only one country

825
00:45:05.077 --> 00:45:06.870
that survives until the end…

826
00:45:09.623 --> 00:45:11.333
will be crowned

827
00:45:12.042 --> 00:45:14.753
the country that embodies

828
00:45:16.797 --> 00:45:19.174
the most perfect physique.

829
00:45:23.846 --> 00:45:25.305
Now,

830
00:45:26.098 --> 00:45:27.933
please change into your uniforms.

831
00:45:40.028 --> 00:45:41.238
We're all getting changed and…

832
00:45:41.321 --> 00:45:44.450
It made me feel like,
"Okay, it's really happening."

833
00:45:44.533 --> 00:45:45.576
"We're really here."

834
00:45:45.659 --> 00:45:49.413
You could see a clear shift
in everyone's eyes.

835
00:45:50.998 --> 00:45:54.418
When I saw the uniform
bearing the Philippine flag…

836
00:45:56.086 --> 00:45:57.880
I felt a huge surge of pride.

837
00:45:59.214 --> 00:46:02.593
I really felt like
I was representing my country.

838
00:46:04.011 --> 00:46:05.888
I was brimming with patriotism.

839
00:46:09.224 --> 00:46:12.728
I'm here to be
the best representative of my country.

840
00:46:13.604 --> 00:46:15.439
Go, Indonesia, bro.

841
00:46:16.023 --> 00:46:19.193
It's an intense feeling of pride.

842
00:46:20.444 --> 00:46:24.072
It's important to uphold
the honor of your country.

843
00:46:34.500 --> 00:46:36.543
Physical: Asia.

844
00:46:37.836 --> 00:46:38.962
You are all gathered here today

845
00:46:39.546 --> 00:46:43.258
to prove which country embodies

846
00:46:43.800 --> 00:46:45.302
the most perfect physique.

847
00:46:47.679 --> 00:46:51.308
If a contestant is unable to
carry out the quests

848
00:46:51.391 --> 00:46:54.645
due to injury
or any other unforeseen circumstances,

849
00:46:55.187 --> 00:46:57.105
they will be replaced by a substitute.

850
00:46:58.565 --> 00:47:01.610
The one country to survive until the end

851
00:47:03.111 --> 00:47:04.196
will win…

852
00:47:15.541 --> 00:47:16.875
one billion…

853
00:47:17.793 --> 00:47:18.627
one billion…

854
00:47:19.503 --> 00:47:21.129
one billion won.

855
00:47:23.382 --> 00:47:25.217
That's crazy.

856
00:47:30.138 --> 00:47:31.640
Wow, a billion won?

857
00:47:33.267 --> 00:47:34.560
Let's take that home.

858
00:47:35.394 --> 00:47:37.396
Holy moly.

859
00:47:37.938 --> 00:47:39.314
That's insane.

860
00:47:40.357 --> 00:47:41.441
That much?

861
00:47:41.984 --> 00:47:43.110
One billion won.

862
00:47:44.069 --> 00:47:45.112
Come on, let's get it.

863
00:47:48.949 --> 00:47:53.495
May you survive until the end.

864
00:47:57.207 --> 00:48:00.168
Each team leader
will now give a short battle speech.

865
00:48:01.420 --> 00:48:04.298
Team Leader of the Republic of Korea,
Kim Dong-hyun.

866
00:48:05.340 --> 00:48:08.260
I believe physical ability
stems from the mind.

867
00:48:08.343 --> 00:48:10.804
Since Koreans possess
unmatched mental fortitude,

868
00:48:10.887 --> 00:48:13.640
that inner strength
will drive us to victory.

869
00:48:18.437 --> 00:48:20.355
Japan is the land of martial arts.

870
00:48:20.439 --> 00:48:22.774
It is also a sports powerhouse.

871
00:48:22.858 --> 00:48:27.362
Through Physical: Asia,
we will prove our strength.

872
00:48:27.446 --> 00:48:29.364
Bring it on!

873
00:48:33.785 --> 00:48:37.372
We flew 11 hours
to reach Korea from Türkiye.

874
00:48:37.456 --> 00:48:39.625
We're not here just to have fun.

875
00:48:39.708 --> 00:48:41.877
We are Turkish.
We are strong. We are ready.

876
00:48:41.960 --> 00:48:43.754
-That's what I'm talking about!
-Bravo.

877
00:48:44.671 --> 00:48:48.759
All our team members are full of
the fighting spirit rooted in Muay Thai.

878
00:48:48.842 --> 00:48:50.636
And with that spirit,

879
00:48:50.719 --> 00:48:53.513
we will prevail
as the victors of this competition.

880
00:48:53.597 --> 00:48:56.850
Mongolians are descendants
of Genghis Khan.

881
00:48:56.933 --> 00:48:59.561
We will show you
the might of the Mongol sword.

882
00:49:00.437 --> 00:49:01.855
We didn't come here to play games,

883
00:49:01.938 --> 00:49:03.815
we came here to win at all costs.

884
00:49:03.899 --> 00:49:05.734
And we're gonna run through
anyone that gets in our way.

885
00:49:05.817 --> 00:49:08.403
We have one goal,

886
00:49:08.487 --> 00:49:09.738
victory!

887
00:49:10.614 --> 00:49:12.741
Filipinos have champion blood,

888
00:49:12.824 --> 00:49:16.286
so we'll make sure that we get the crown.

889
00:49:16.370 --> 00:49:19.122
-Let's fight!
-Let's go, Philippines!

890
00:49:20.832 --> 00:49:22.376
The legend speaks.

891
00:49:27.714 --> 00:49:29.299
Physical: Asia.

892
00:49:30.884 --> 00:49:33.887
The first quest will now begin.

893
00:49:34.513 --> 00:49:36.264
Please give your best

894
00:49:36.890 --> 00:49:38.684
for the honor of your country.

895
00:49:40.102 --> 00:49:43.730
It's gonna be an all-out war
against all the other Asian countries.

896
00:49:43.814 --> 00:49:45.691
I wanted to show them
how dangerous we are.

897
00:49:45.774 --> 00:49:47.734
I wanted them to fear us.

898
00:49:47.818 --> 00:49:50.946
I see us being
a very strong contender to win this.

899
00:50:47.961 --> 00:50:54.634
QUEST: 1

900
00:51:07.105 --> 00:51:08.815
Physical: Asia.

901
00:51:08.899 --> 00:51:10.317
All contestants,

902
00:51:10.984 --> 00:51:13.862
please enter the arena.

903
00:51:18.617 --> 00:51:21.161
Wow, what do we have here?

904
00:51:21.244 --> 00:51:23.580
-Sand? Why is there sand?
-Sand?

905
00:51:26.416 --> 00:51:28.335
Man, what's going on here?

906
00:51:29.711 --> 00:51:30.796
There's the big mound.

907
00:51:30.879 --> 00:51:32.798
-All right, we're climbing up a hill.
-Yup.

908
00:51:32.881 --> 00:51:34.174
What the hell?

909
00:51:35.258 --> 00:51:38.386
Oh my gosh, this is amazing.

910
00:51:38.470 --> 00:51:39.679
Huh? What is this?

911
00:51:39.763 --> 00:51:41.014
It's sand.

912
00:51:41.097 --> 00:51:42.724
Oh, I like the look of this.

913
00:51:42.808 --> 00:51:45.018
It's like the desert in Dune.

914
00:51:47.437 --> 00:51:48.980
What on earth is this?

915
00:51:49.064 --> 00:51:50.398
Holy shit.

916
00:51:53.068 --> 00:51:55.237
It was intimidating.
There was a huge mound of sand.

917
00:51:55.320 --> 00:51:57.989
Are we meant to transport all this sand?

918
00:51:58.073 --> 00:52:00.534
Do we run around it?

919
00:52:00.617 --> 00:52:02.077
Or is it a strength contest?

920
00:52:02.160 --> 00:52:04.412
Especially being a heavy athlete,

921
00:52:04.496 --> 00:52:06.665
in the sand, might be a bit tricky.

922
00:52:08.250 --> 00:52:09.584
The first quest is…

923
00:52:13.213 --> 00:52:15.090
the territory conquest.

924
00:52:15.924 --> 00:52:17.843
…the territory conquest.

925
00:52:19.511 --> 00:52:20.554
Conquest?

926
00:52:21.137 --> 00:52:22.222
Shit.

927
00:52:22.305 --> 00:52:23.723
Oh, what's going on?

928
00:52:25.100 --> 00:52:26.935
-Oh, here we go.
-Oh, sick.

929
00:52:33.650 --> 00:52:35.402
The sun's rising.

930
00:52:36.027 --> 00:52:37.946
-The sun's rising.
-It sure is.

931
00:52:45.036 --> 00:52:46.580
In the territory conquest,

932
00:52:47.163 --> 00:52:49.082
all eight countries
will start simultaneously

933
00:52:50.208 --> 00:52:52.210
and compete to conquer the territories

934
00:52:52.794 --> 00:52:54.421
on top of the sand dune.

935
00:52:55.463 --> 00:52:56.715
Simultaneously.

936
00:52:57.549 --> 00:52:59.426
We have to fight for the top position.

937
00:53:00.260 --> 00:53:01.720
-So it's a full-on contact sport.
-Sorry?

938
00:53:01.803 --> 00:53:03.388
-It's a full-on contact sport.
-Yes, it is.

939
00:53:03.471 --> 00:53:06.683
I was thinking,
"Physical: Asia has begun for real."

940
00:53:06.766 --> 00:53:09.019
"We can finally fight."

941
00:53:09.102 --> 00:53:10.145
YUSHIN OKAMI
MMA FIGHTER

942
00:53:10.228 --> 00:53:11.813
It got me really fired up.

943
00:53:11.897 --> 00:53:13.690
IGEDZ EXECUTIONER
BODYBUILDER

944
00:53:13.773 --> 00:53:16.735
To be honest, we didn't realize
teamwork would be required.

945
00:53:16.818 --> 00:53:18.695
In the previous seasons,

946
00:53:18.778 --> 00:53:24.200
the first quest had always been
individual events.

947
00:53:24.284 --> 00:53:29.831
So this challenge
came as a complete surprise.

948
00:53:30.457 --> 00:53:33.835
Here are the rules
of the territory conquest.

949
00:53:35.670 --> 00:53:37.339
-Oh, there are four.
-I see.

950
00:53:37.422 --> 00:53:40.717
The first quest, the territory conquest,

951
00:53:41.384 --> 00:53:44.137
will consist of a total of three rounds.

952
00:53:48.183 --> 00:53:51.436
The first round of the first quest,

953
00:53:51.519 --> 00:53:52.854
the territory conquest.

954
00:53:53.980 --> 00:53:56.358
There will be four territories,

955
00:53:58.401 --> 00:54:00.737
and each round will last for two minutes.

956
00:54:02.656 --> 00:54:04.157
Two minutes. That's short.

957
00:54:04.658 --> 00:54:06.117
So it's about speed.

958
00:54:06.201 --> 00:54:07.953
At the end of the round,

959
00:54:08.036 --> 00:54:12.165
the country with the most contestants
on a given territory

960
00:54:12.707 --> 00:54:14.918
will conquer that territory.

961
00:54:15.919 --> 00:54:18.171
-That's really simple.
-This will get really physical.

962
00:54:19.005 --> 00:54:21.841
We need as many of us as possible
to end up on the round platform.

963
00:54:21.925 --> 00:54:23.510
In two minutes. That's tricky.

964
00:54:23.593 --> 00:54:25.345
-Because we want the numbers--
-Have as many people as we can

965
00:54:25.428 --> 00:54:26.471
on the territory at the end.

966
00:54:26.554 --> 00:54:27.639
We want everyone.

967
00:54:28.181 --> 00:54:29.933
This game

968
00:54:30.016 --> 00:54:33.228
will involve shoving,
grabbing, and grappling.

969
00:54:35.605 --> 00:54:39.401
I've never collided or had contact
with anyone in sports,

970
00:54:39.484 --> 00:54:41.695
so this was more brutal than I'd expected.

971
00:54:41.778 --> 00:54:42.779
I hate this kind of game.

972
00:54:42.862 --> 00:54:44.406
Contact sports are totally not my jam.

973
00:54:44.489 --> 00:54:45.573
I was confident.

974
00:54:45.657 --> 00:54:48.493
I'm a ssireum wrestler,
so I figured tussling on the sand

975
00:54:48.576 --> 00:54:50.161
would totally be my forte.

976
00:54:50.245 --> 00:54:51.663
ADIYASUREN
NATIONAL TEAM JUDOKA

977
00:54:51.746 --> 00:54:53.540
It looked kind of easy.

978
00:54:53.623 --> 00:54:57.293
I thought it was a game
that would play to my strengths.

979
00:54:57.377 --> 00:54:59.879
The four countries
that manage to conquer a territory

980
00:54:59.963 --> 00:55:02.007
will advance to the next round.

981
00:55:03.675 --> 00:55:05.468
In the second round,
the number of territories

982
00:55:05.552 --> 00:55:06.720
will be reduced to two.

983
00:55:08.847 --> 00:55:11.307
And in the third and final round,

984
00:55:11.391 --> 00:55:13.351
there will only be one single territory.

985
00:55:16.521 --> 00:55:20.108
The country that conquers
this last remaining territory

986
00:55:21.109 --> 00:55:24.529
will be the winner of the first quest,

987
00:55:25.071 --> 00:55:26.865
the territory conquest.

988
00:55:28.158 --> 00:55:30.618
However, if a territory is occupied
by the same number of contestants

989
00:55:30.702 --> 00:55:32.370
from more than one country,

990
00:55:33.204 --> 00:55:36.458
the match will go into overtime
on that territory.

991
00:55:37.792 --> 00:55:41.212
So it's basically musical chairs.

992
00:55:41.296 --> 00:55:43.506
Just without any dancing.

993
00:55:43.590 --> 00:55:44.799
Three rounds,

994
00:55:44.883 --> 00:55:46.009
so pace yourselves.

995
00:55:46.092 --> 00:55:47.594
We want the first round.

996
00:55:48.261 --> 00:55:51.347
The country that wins
the territory conquest

997
00:55:52.223 --> 00:55:54.893
will gain a significant privilege.

998
00:55:55.977 --> 00:55:57.562
What? Gain a significant what?

999
00:55:59.397 --> 00:56:00.857
Wait, he's just about to tell us.

1000
00:56:00.940 --> 00:56:02.734
The significant privilege is…

1001
00:56:12.243 --> 00:56:13.411
the right to set

1002
00:56:14.329 --> 00:56:18.541
the matchups for the following quest.

1003
00:56:19.667 --> 00:56:21.753
Man, this is huge.

1004
00:56:22.295 --> 00:56:24.339
You will set the matchups

1005
00:56:24.422 --> 00:56:28.051
for all the countries including your own.

1006
00:56:28.134 --> 00:56:29.636
So it's a knockout tournament again.

1007
00:56:29.719 --> 00:56:31.971
Oh, we can make… We can pick…

1008
00:56:32.055 --> 00:56:33.014
-Oh, yes.
-Yeah, yeah.

1009
00:56:33.098 --> 00:56:35.475
-We can handpick this comp, dude.
-Yeah.

1010
00:56:35.558 --> 00:56:37.018
Here are the instructions

1011
00:56:37.644 --> 00:56:40.480
regarding the starting point.

1012
00:56:46.194 --> 00:56:49.948
Each team leader must place their hand

1013
00:56:50.031 --> 00:56:53.284
on their chosen flagpole base
before the others.

1014
00:56:54.160 --> 00:56:55.578
Indonesia's the weakest here.

1015
00:56:55.662 --> 00:56:57.413
-We go for Indonesia.
-All right.

1016
00:56:57.497 --> 00:56:58.373
JUSTIN COVENEY
NATIONAL TEAM RUGBY PLAYER

1017
00:56:58.456 --> 00:57:00.041
If you look at Indonesia's lineup,

1018
00:57:00.125 --> 00:57:02.085
it's quite mixed,
just like the Philippines.

